      "text": "We start by expressing each logarithm using the change of base formula: $\\log_x 4=\\frac{\\log 4}{\\log x}$ and $\\log_{27} 3=\\frac{\\log 3}{\\log 27}$. Simplifying both sides gives us $\\frac{\\log 4}{\\log x}=\\frac{\\log 3}{3\\log 3}=1$.\n\nTo isolate $\\log x$, we take the reciprocal of both sides: $\\log x=\\log 4$.\n\nFinally, we convert to the exponential form by taking $e^{\\log x}$ and $e^{\\log 4}$, which gives us $x=e^{\\log 4}=\\boxed{4}$. The answer is: 4",
